Like, Lord of the Rings being about the Third Age of Middle-earth, and the elves are leaving and All the great kingdoms are gone, and it's really this dying world that had a former glory, and it's just a change and a deterioration. And this is already kind of the Catholic worldview, uh, at least back then.

00:13:38.941 --> 00:14:01.976
So as a polar opposite, the alchemist had a very strong view into the world to not discount the earthly things, but to focus on them extremely. And C.G. Jung noticed this connection to Christianity very often. And I will talk more about it once I've laid a little bit more foundation.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:22.408
So alchemy, outward-oriented to the material world, to the things happening in the earthly realm. And this idea of all the things that happen above, outside, also happening inside in the small.

