Just we had New Year's Eve and we have the rockets and everything, and they have different colors. This is based on what kind of metals are in there. Based on the metal, you have green, you have red, you have yellow, and so on. So today we know all this because we had all this scientific endeavor and it becomes usual for us because, because we have seen it so often.

00:18:55.901 --> 00:19:18.131
It's very weird when you have no idea what's happening, but suddenly you take one material and the flame becomes green. It's a little bit like magic. And this is what alchemists did, just combining things and seeing how things interacted and seeing changes like the flames. Changing the color just by taking different materials.

00:19:18.889 --> 00:19:43.479
And there was no explanation really for that. It just seemed like magic. And as they're toiling away, the alchemists, they have this idea of the opus magnum opus, this great work, so that they're working on something very specific and important. And this is the freeing of the material potential.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:20:06.030
Into the world. And the goal that is there, commonly it's referred to as gold, but the alchemist called it lapis. And this was the idea to create the lapis through the great work that they did.

00:20:07.114 --> 00:20:27.053
And of course they documented this and tried to document it. And here Jung noticed that there was no— on one side, every alchemist had their own terminology, they had their own symbols, their own terms, how to describe things.

